WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:01.810
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:06.160
about free training, automation,
and optimizing storage costs.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.410
I'm Stephanie Wong, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.770
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.833
There's not much
better than free.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.250
Since the start
of the year, we've

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.560
introduced a number of
opportunities for you

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.560
to grow your skills, and we
wanted to bring them together

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.100
into one place.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.100
Whether you're just getting
started on the Cloud

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.100
or are looking for ways to
challenge yourself and collect

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.070
skills badges, bookmark
this collection of training

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.960
opportunities and
check back regularly

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.420
Automation is now
available for everyone

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.250
with AppSheet automation.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.770
AppSheet, our no-code
development platform,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.200
leverages Google AI
to make it easier

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.390
to automate business
processes, letting

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:50.220
you focus more on high-impact
work and less on manual tasks.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.100
Check out the Getting Started
video and reclaim your time.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.440
Storage is a
critical component of

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.300
any cloud-based infrastructure.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.820
Without a place to store
and serve your data,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.970
databases won't work,
compute can't run,

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.000
and networks have nowhere to
put the data they're carrying.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.980
So it's no surprise
that you want

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.950
to make sure you're
optimizing your storage costs.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.810
This guide will give
you advice on what

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:19.470
to look for and identify
ways you can save some cash.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.510
Sometimes a picture is
worth a thousand words,

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.080
and that's where these
cheat sheets come in handy.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.410
Our own Priyanka Vergadia
has built a number of guides

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.990
that help developers visually
navigate critical decisions,

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.560
whether it's determining the
best way to move to the cloud

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.620
or deciding on the
best storage options.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.990
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.550
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.660
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.230
We'll see you in the cloud.

